            <ArticleTitle>Uterine actinomycosis associated with an enterocutaneous fistula. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A postmenopausal woman with suppurative actinomycotic uterine infection complicated by an enterocutaneous fistula is reported. It occurred against a background of prolonged use of an intra-uterine contraceptive device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
